abstract='This dissertation investigates whether large language models can identify security misconfigurations in Terraform configurations for Amazon Web Services and provide useful remediations. The planned method compares GPT-4o, Claude Sonnet 4.6, and Gemini 2.5 Pro under zero-shot and few-shot prompting against findings from Checkov and Trivy. The current empirical material is limited to the TerraGoat AWS module. Checkov reported 215 Terraform findings and Trivy reported 113. Because the tools use different policy identifiers, a documented manual semantic crosswalk yielded 75 deduplicated candidate consensus groups at the file and resource level. This crosswalk is provisional and requires independent review. No LLM API responses, GitHub corpus, or Terraform Registry modules are included in the present draft. Consequently, model precision, recall, F1-score, category-level detection performance, and remediation quality have not been measured, and the three research questions remain open. The draft reports the observed static analysis results and defines the work needed to complete the proposed evaluation without presenting unmeasured model performance as a finding.'
before(first_ch,'Abstract','Heading 1',align=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER,bold=True)
